\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 InlineArray
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  is a statically-sized, stack-allocated array, so it's a fast and efficient way to allocate storage for most kinds of 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 LayoutTensor
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . There are target-dependent limits on how much memory can be allocated this way, however.\
You can also create a 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 LayoutTensor
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  using an 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 UnsafePointer
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . This may be preferable for very large tensors.\
